        },
        {
          "name": "iconName",
          "tags": [],
          "docs": "The drawable resource name for the button icon (WITHOUT file extension).\n\n**Android:** Place icon files in `android/app/src/main/res/drawable/`.\n- Format: Vector XML (24dp) or PNG (48×48px for mdpi, 96×96px for xhdpi)\n- Naming: Use lowercase with underscores, e.g. `ic_shuffle.xml`\n- The plugin resolves by trying: exact name → `ic_<name>` → `ms_<name>`\n- Example: `iconName: 'ic_shuffle'` → looks for `res/drawable/ic_shuffle.xml`\n- Example: `iconName: 'shuffle'` → looks for `res/drawable/shuffle.xml`,\n  then `res/drawable/ic_shuffle.xml`, then `res/drawable/ms_shuffle.xml`\n\n**iOS:** SF Symbol name (e.g., 'heart', 'shuffle').\n\n**Tip:** You can use Android Studio's Vector Asset tool to import Material\nIcons directly as XML drawables.",
          "complexTypes": [],
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "enabled",
          "tags": [],
          "docs": "Whether the button is enabled/visible. Default: true",
          "complexTypes": [],
          "type": "boolean | undefined"
        },
        {
          "name": "position",
          "tags": [],
          "docs": "Position of the button relative to transport controls.\n- `'left'`: Displayed BEFORE the Previous button\n- `'right'`: Displayed AFTER the Next button\nDefault: `'right'`",
